    <briefdescription>
<para>Post-assembly functor that pins a set of cells to prescribed values. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>For every constrained cell c: <ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref>[c, j] = 0 for j != c (zero row off-diagonals) <ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref>[j, c] = 0 for j != c (zero column in neighbour rows, rhs[j] absorbs the dropped term) rhs[c] = <ref refid="classA" kindref="compound">A</ref>[c,c] * value[c]</para>
<para>Pinning via both the row and column cut avoids large cancellation errors when pinned values are orders of magnitude larger than neighbouring unknowns. Off-rank coupling in offDiagonalMatrix is also zeroed for pinned rows.</para>
<para>Restricted to scalar ValueType: the segregated vector-solve path dispatches through <ref refid="structNeoN_1_1dsl_1_1PostAssemblyBase_1af0170570aa68740698ac111b485cc18c" kindref="member">applyScalarMatrix()</ref>, which this class does not implement.</para>
<para>mask[cell] != 0 marks a constrained cell; value[cell] holds its target. Both views are sized nCells and must outlive the functor. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
